 \"When did John Oscroft begin his career in cricket?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 109, \"text\": \"John Oscroft (cricketer, born 1807) John Oscroft (21 July 1807 – 28 September 1857) was an English cricketer.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 110, \"end\": 159, \"text\": \"Oscroft's batting and bowling styles are unknown.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 160, \"end\": 199, \"text\": \"He was born at Arnold, Nottinghamshire.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 200, \"end\": 317, \"text\": \"Oscroft made his first-class debut for Nottingham Cricket Club against Cambridge Town Club in 1834 at Parker's Piece.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 318, \"end\": 531, \"text\": \"He made two further first-class appearances in 1834, making a second appearance against Cambridge Town Club at the Forest New Ground and an appearance against Sheffield Cricket Club at Hyde Park Ground, Sheffield.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"start\": 532, \"end\": 655, \"text\": \"His next first-class appearance came in 1842 for the Gentlemen of Nottinghamshire against the Players of Nottinghamshire at\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 166, \"text\": \"John Oscroft (cricketer, born 1846) John Thomas Oscroft (1846-1885) was an English cricketer who played first-class cricket for Nottinghamshire between 1867 and 1874.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 167, \"end\": 255, \"text\": \"He was the brother of William Oscroft, who later captained Nottinghamshire from 1881-82.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 256, \"end\": 353, \"text\": \"Oscroft made his first-class debut in an 1867 County Match for Nottinghamshire against Middlesex.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 354, \"end\": 380, \"text\": \"He made scores of 0 and 3.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 381, \"end\": 474, \"text\": \"In 1868, Oscroft made an appearance for Beeston Cricket Club against Wirksworth Cricket Club.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 475, \"end\": 532, \"text\": \"Oscroft score 0 opening the batting, ad took two wickets.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"start\": 533, \"end\": 654, \"text\": \"The following year, Oscroft represented the All England Eleven along with his brother William; the match against a United\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 1, \"text\": \".\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d02\", \"start\": 2, \"end\": 206, \"text\": \"Privacy policy About Wikipedia Disclaimers Contact Wikipedia Code of Conduct Developers Statistics Cookie statement Mobile view Search Search Toggle the table of contents Eric Oscroft 1 language Add topic\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"Hambledon/Hampshire team during Small 's prime years can be seen in the team being rated the ( unofficial ) Champion County in 10 seasons : 1766–1771 , 1776–1777 , 1779 and 1783 .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d03\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 289, \"text\": \"He died at Petersfield , where he was in residence for most of his life and where he established businesses .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d03\", \"start\": 290, \"end\": 534, \"text\": \"Small was a very influential player who was involved in the creation of two significant permanent additions to the Laws of Cricket : the maximum width of the bat and the introduction of the middle stump ( out of the three stumps ) of the wicket\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Oscroft\", \"scope\": \"first-class cricket debut\", \"claim\": \"John Oscroft made his first-class debut for Nottingham Cricket Club against Cambridge Town Club in 1834 at Parker's Piece.\", \"answer\": \"1834\", \"quote\": \"Oscroft made his first-class debut for Nottingham Cricket Club against Cambridge Town Club in 1834 at Parker's Piece.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0277-126485321eb1:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"John Oscroft\", \"scope\": \"cricket career debut\", \"claim\": \"John Oscroft made his first-class debut in 1867.\", \"answer\": \"1867\", \"quote\": \"John Oscroft (cricketer, born 1846) John Thomas Oscroft (1846-1885) was an English cricketer who played first-class cricket for Nottinghamshire between 1867 and 1874. He was the brother of William Oscroft, who later captained Nottinghamshire from 1881-82. Oscroft made his first-class debut in an 1867 County Match for Nottinghamshire against Middlesex.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"1834\", \"1867\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"1834\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"1867\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}], \"fallible_audits\": {\"J_A\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S4\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"death_date\", \"ent